                    {
                        "name":  "places/ChIJ22KOy-irQjQRnrFOQj_aanw/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xGaGNXZFNkVVpVU0hRMFJWRlNlRWQ0T1RsRWFVRRAB",
                        "relativePublishTimeDescription":  "10 months ago",
                        "rating":  3,
                        "text":  {
                                     "text":  "As a longtime fan of Gonna EAT, I came to GonnaPLUS with high expectations—but I’m honestly disappointed.\n\nFirst, the service was unexpectedly poor. Staff members were unfriendly and looked visibly annoyed throughout the visit. Second, while the restroom clearly had thoughtful design elements and aesthetic intent, it was unfortunately dirty and had a strong odor, which ruined the experience.\n\nAs for the food: while the flavor remained consistent with the Gonna brand, the portion size was noticeably smaller than at Gonna EAT. The price point didn’t reflect any upgrade in quality—except for the plating, which did feel more “PLUS,” but not enough to justify the difference.\n\nOverall, I had hoped for a premium Gonna experience, but instead left feeling underwhelmed.",
                                     "languageCode":  "en"
                                 },
                        "originalText":  {
